I have submitted PR that fixes an issue where it was impossible to add drops to preexisting mobs #40.
But to exactly match zombie and skellies (and possibly even more if mod devs extend vanilla entitites) you will want to add logic similar to NER (method below).

Wasn't sure where exactly you would want to put this. My thought given that probably I am the first one using addDrops is to add the logic in MobRegistry.addDrops and have mod devs pass in entity instance from which you can read everything you need. On the other hand I feel that in this class you would want to always exact match so perhaps the only additional bit of info needed is for wither skelly. (but I may be missing something regarding the exact match)

```
public Set<MobEntry> getRegistryMatches(Class clazz, boolean exactMatch, boolean witherSkeleton)
{
    Set<MobEntry> result = new LinkedHashSet<MobEntry>();
    int wither = witherSkeleton ? 1 : 0;
    for (MobEntry regEntry : registry)
    {
        Set classes = new LinkedHashSet();
        if (exactMatch) classes.add(regEntry.getEntity().getClass());
        else classes = ClassScraper.getGeneralizations(regEntry.getEntity().getClass());
        for (Object generalClass : classes)
        {
            if (generalClass == clazz)
            {
                if (exactMatch && clazz == EntitySkeleton.class)
                    if (((EntitySkeleton) regEntry.getEntity()).getSkeletonType() != wither) break;
                result.add(regEntry);
            }
        }
    }
    return result;
}
```
